{
  "problem": {
    "title": "Production Line Activation MIP: Maximize Profit with Fixed Setup Costs",
    "description": "A factory can produce 3 products (A1, A2, A3) in a month (22 working days). Each product has a maximum market demand, net profit margin, daily production quota, a fixed activation cost if the production line is started, and a minimum batch size if activated. Decide whether to activate each product's line and how much to produce to maximize total profit (revenue minus production cost minus activation cost).",
    "problem_type": "mixed_integer_programming",
    "objective": "maximize",
    "objective_description": "Total profit = sum over products of (margin[p] * produce[p] - activation_cost[p] * activate[p])",
    "constraints": [
      {
        "description": "Working day limit: sum over products of produce[p] * days_per_unit[p] <= 22 (total production days cannot exceed 22)"
      },
      {
        "description": "Production capacity: if activated, max produce = min(22*quota, max_demand); if not activated, produce = 0"
      },
      {
        "description": "Minimum batch: if activated, produce >= min_batch"
      },
      {
        "description": "Demand cap: produce[p] <= max_demand[p]"
      }
    ],
    "decision_variables": [
      "produce[p]: units of product p produced (continuous, non-negative)",
      "activate[p]: 1 if product p line is activated, 0 otherwise (binary)"
    ],
    "parameters": [
      "margin[p]: net profit per unit produced (selling price - production cost)",
      "quota[p]: max units per day if all 22 days devoted to product p",
      "activation_cost[p]: fixed cost to activate product p's line",
      "min_batch[p]: minimum units if product p is activated",
      "max_demand[p]: maximum market demand for product p",
      "big_m[p]: min(22*quota[p], max_demand[p]) used as big-M coefficient",
      "days_per_unit[p]: 1/quota[p], days consumed per unit of product p produced"
    ],
    "additional_notes": "Products: A1 (margin=50.70, quota=500, activation=170000, min_batch=20, max_demand=5300, days_per_unit=0.002), A2 (margin=56.10, quota=450, activation=150000, min_batch=20, max_demand=4500, days_per_unit=0.002222), A3 (margin=49.60, quota=550, activation=100000, min_batch=16, max_demand=5400, days_per_unit=0.001818). big_m = min(22*quota, max_demand): A1=5300, A2=4500, A3=5400. Key binding constraint: sum(produce[p]/quota[p]) <= 22. All 3 at max demand requires 5300/500+4500/450+5400/550=10.6+10+9.82=30.42 days (infeasible). Optimal: activate only A2+A3 at max demand. Days used=4500/450+5400/550=10+9.82=19.82 <= 22. Profit=56.10*4500+49.60*5400-150000-100000=252450+267840-250000=270290. Obj=270290.",
    "csv_file_paths": {
      "products": "products.csv"
    }
  },
